		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4158&amp;p=32774#p32774"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Im not sure but the old MD9600 I have does seem to be too narrow on receive for FM stations on 2m running narrow deviation on transmit.. I get distortion and audio cut out when trying to receive these stations . Is there any way of making the receive on 2m FM slightly wider than it is please ? ...apart from setting my rig to 25Khz on receive. I have never used a deviation meter , this is going by ear and the other stations reports.</div></blockquote>I tested my MD-9600 V2 on TX deviation with a Marconi TF2304 and it seems that my MD-9600 is a bit narrower on both 2.5 and 5 kHz deviation, I also compared to a RT3S and a Yaesu FT-817DN and those was more or less 2.5 and 5 kHz on NFM and FM.<br><br>But my meter isn't calibrated for many years but I have verified it against my Marconi 2022D signalgenerator which I've verified via Bessel null so I don't think the deviation meter is so bad.<br><br>I also noticed that the MD-9600 seems a bit to narrow on RX but I don't know how to verify that via some measurement yet.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Fri Sep 06, 2024 11:39 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
