		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4158&amp;p=32548#p32548"><![CDATA[
That resistor is the factory mod to improve the volume control. It is an old trick to change the slope of a potentiometer from linear to something closer to log law. <br><br>I originally suggested the mod with a 1K resistor but the factory decided to change that to 2K2. I still think 1K works better. <br><br>If you think it is bad now you should have tried it before they started fitting the mod! <br><br>I am still surprised that they have never changed to the proper log law pot. I can only assume it is a component supply or cost saving issue. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Sun Aug 18, 2024 9:15 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
