		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4158&amp;p=31910#p31910"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I've tested my MD-9600 with a small monitor speaker ( Audio Pro Avantek Onehouse ) but they have maybe to much bass performance.<br><br>I've ordered another radio communication speaker from amazon ( "Diamond TS 750" ) which has some -6 dB mute and some sort of filter built in .</div></blockquote>I have used the "Diamond TS 750" speaker some time now and for me it sound better compared to the built-in one which had some rattle and resonance problems in my installation.<br><br>But I doubt that the one I bought from amazon.se is a genuine Diamond and the buttons doesn't do as they should according to the markings.<br>The "MUTE (-8db)" is only an on/off switch and the "NOISE FILTER" maybe remove some noise but it mostly attenuate the sound.<br>( Filter consists of a RC filter with a 50 Ohm resistor and a 47 uF electrolytic )<br>I will probably experiment with it and change the wiring a bit later.<br><br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2486&amp;sid=42c08e720ca96a696a107c8c977727df" class="postimage" alt="Capture.JPG" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><br>Note the bare wires:<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2487&amp;sid=42c08e720ca96a696a107c8c977727df" class="postimage" alt="Capture2.JPG" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Wed Jul 03, 2024 10:10 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
