		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: MD-9600 Receive Audio, how to improve?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4158&amp;p=31853#p31853"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Interestingly, this is not an issue on analog FM receive. </div></blockquote>The audio path for both DMR and FM goes through the same pot, so the rate of change of audio level, controlled by the pot, will be the same for both FM and DMR<br><br>There is also an option , in Sound options, to enable a form of audio AGC on DMR and set the default AGC gain level, which may improve things for you your specific case<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Jun 28, 2024 1:48 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
